etString, which is what the lookup reads. Added tests for: the future default, a device setting that affects only that device, a device setting that overrides the config, a device setting of 0 that turns off the future default, a group setting with a device override, and per-device minPeriod and dailyLimit."},{"path":"docs/harness/log.md","summary":"Added a log entry for this change."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"A filter setting on a device or group changes the filtering of that device only","met":true,"evidence":"In FilterHandlerTest, testDeviceAttribute, testDeviceAttributeOverridesConfig, testDeviceAttributeDisablesFutureDefault, testGroupAttribute, testDeviceMinPeriod and testDeviceDailyLimit each check that the configured device is filtered (or not) while a second device with no setting behaves differently."},{"criterion":"The change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"make test TESTS=org.traccar.handler.FilterHandlerTest: 10 tests run, 0 failures."},{"criterion":"The existing test suite still passes","met":true,"evidence":"make check-fast: Checkstyle main and test pass, 620 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 27 skipped (tests that were already disabled), BUILD SUCCESSFUL. make check (the full CI build) was not run."}],"human_needed":[],"harness_used":["AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md: commands table (make test TESTS=..., make check-fast) and the rule that every config key lives in Keys.java with Javadoc","implement-change skill: names FilterHandler and FilterHandlerTest as the example pair and gives the test-first steps","docs/harness/log.md: the log-entry convention","make check-fast: fast, reliable gate (about 12 s with a warm cache)"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":"docs/architecture.md","problem":"Does not explain how per-device settings are resolved (KeyType.DEVICE plus AttributeUtil.lookup: device, then groups, then server, then config, then default). I learned it by reading AttributeUtil."},{"file":"src/test/java/org/traccar/BaseTest.java","problem":"There is no test helper that builds a CacheManager mock with a device, groups and config values for AttributeUtil.lookup. Tests must know that the lookup calls Config.getString(key) and not getBoolean or getLong. That is easy to get wrong, and the old FilterHandlerTest mocks would have stopped working without any error."},{"file":"traccar-web (submodule)","problem":"The submodule is empty in this checkout, so I could not check whether the web UI lists the new device attributes."}]},"ttft_ms":1397,"type":"result","duration_ms":135960,"uuid":"f442c97c-239b-4e66-a60a-13038eb6c229","ttft_stream_ms":1318,"time_to_request_ms":122,"first_content_frame_ms":1318,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":13778,"cacheReadInputTokens":585310,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42958,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.73639,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1286,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":42958,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
